From cd5acf97e10b7d684b0cb2dff47c3bb90dcff74e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ILFforever <hammymukura@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:42:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] X-H2 playback: SD DMA to the declared DRAM limit, JPEG
 blocks and playback stubs

- 25-sd: ram_bytes = 0xf0000000, the board's [dram] limit (RAM 0+0x80000000
  and 0x80000000+0x70000000). Playback of an SD picture DMAs to 0xeec00000,
  which the old 0x80000000 limit refused.
- 52-jpeg / 58-playback: the JPEG encoder and decoder, declared as on the
  X-T5. Playback of a slot 2 picture writes the decoder (+0x118) first.
- 57-develop-playback-port: the X-T5's develop/playback completion stubs and
  helper blocks the X-H2 board did not declare (0xffd0c000 resizer and the
  rest). Interrupt lines and constants are the X-T5's, UNVERIFIED on the X-H2.

Verified on 5.20: playback opens a camera JPEG in slot 2 (file number, date,
shooting info shown; the decoder stub draws no pixels), and the playback menu
lists all three pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
